From f42205cdc16ac98f52981fdd09ac9308108e44f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josh Matern <josh.matern@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:58:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Repair appended templates, restore CSRF header on checkout,
 fix /success setup state

- landing.html, success.html, auth/login.html contained two concatenated documents
  (old content appended after new); replaced with the clean rebuild versions.
- Checkout fetch in landing.html and pricing.html lacked the X-CSRFToken header, so
  CSRFProtect rejected every POST with an HTML 400 before /create_checkout ran.
  Header restored; .catch() now reports HTTP status instead of blaming the network.
- _setup_state_for_session treated the 'PENDING_SETUP' placeholder hash as a real
  password, so new customers saw "account ready, log in" with no password set.
  Now mirrors the webhook's placeholder-aware check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0112RzCriTqyJSvH1NucpVG6
